[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956054504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-2956054504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":2956054504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wMc_o","user":{"login":"MYTNB","id":31533351,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTMzMzUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31533351?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB","html_url":"https://github.com/MYTNB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T14:59:03Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T15:09:25Z","body":"I think this should be fixed in godot-cpp. It's not an issue with the engine, I just hope that both parties can reach an agreement.\r\n\r\noh... Besides get_godot_version, there are still many bindings lost, and I think I should give up","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956054504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956095584","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-2956095584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":2956095584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wMnBg","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T15:13:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T15:13:26Z","body":"Did you create [an issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues)? Sometimes, before submitting a PR, perhaps the best idea is to ask if this is considered an issue first. Because you seem to revert a previous behavior and that change was made for a reason.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956095584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956111351","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-2956111351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":2956111351,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wMq33","user":{"login":"MYTNB","id":31533351,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNTMzMzUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31533351?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB","html_url":"https://github.com/MYTNB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MYTNB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T15:19:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T15:19:04Z","body":"> Did you create [an issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues)? Sometimes, before submitting a PR, perhaps the best idea is to ask if this is considered an issue first. Because you seem to revert a previous behavior and that change was made for a reason.\r\n\r\n\r\nSorry, I previously modified the get_godot_version2 method locally and re exported it, but I encountered an issue where array_ref is undefined again\r\n\r\nIt seems that godot_cpp is still using the DISABLE_DEPREGATED method, and I am unable to make simple modifications to fix these issues\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2956111351/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451476878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-4451476878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":4451476878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCVQljg","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T14:16:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T14:16:19Z","body":"_Just stumbled upon this PR, and I wanted to comment about this deprecation at the time but forgot:_\r\n\r\nIf there is one function in the GDExtension API that should **not** have been deprecated, it's `get_godot_version` :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nThis is a foundational API that is often used to query other functionality at runtime. From a compatibility perspective, it's very reasonable to expect that a version check will remain functional until (at least) a potential Godot 5, but now it breaks when run in a newer Godot version compiled with `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`.\r\n\r\nTherefore, the only way to have reliable version checks for an extension is to call _both_ v1 and v2 variants:\r\n- v1 (because v2 isn't available in older versions)\r\n- v2 (because v1 isn't available in newer versions with `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`)\r\n\r\nNote that this is not a possibility for extensions written before v2 was a thing; they will just break, and they can't even dynamically check for an upper bound on supported Godot version at runtime anymore.\r\n\r\nNote also that there was nothing wrong with v1, all v2 did was adding more fields.\r\n\r\nYet it's now also too late to undeprecate, as there are several released Godot versions which no longer support v1 if compiled with `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`. But I think we can learn from this for the future: if we ever add a v3, let's not deprecate v2 :wink: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451476878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045377041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-5045377041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":5045377041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLLpYEQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-22T11:45:14Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T11:45:14Z","body":"> Yet it's now also too late to undeprecate, as there are several released Godot versions which no longer support v1 if compiled with `DISABLE_DEPRECATED`. But I think we can learn from this for the future: if we ever add a v3, let's not deprecate v2 😉\r\n\r\nI don't know that it's too late to undeprecated it? It will be a little awkward, and folks won't be able to 100% rely on it (because it could be missing in custom builds), but if we do decide on a policy of never deprecating the version functions, this would set us up to be consistent with that policy","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5045377041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5058826009","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107329#issuecomment-5058826009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107329","id":5058826009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLYePGQ","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T13:15:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T13:15:41Z","body":"Undeprecating won't change that `get_godot_version` remains an unreliable way to detect versions (on its own), because some Godot releases with custom builds don't have it. So any GDExtension intending to do a **robust** version check must use a combination of `get_godot_version` + `get_godot_version2`.\r\n\r\nIf anything, bringing back `get_godot_version` now will make it worse, because it _looks like_ it's working when testing newer Godot versions, but then it fails for an older range. I'd rather have it fail-fast to make this clear.\r\n\r\nMy takeaway is mainly: `get_godot_version2` should never be deprecated for major version 4.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5058826009/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]